 "Think of a media wall as three projects in one: a furniture piece, an equipment rack and a light fixture. We design all three together. The cabinet run is sized to your receiver, consoles and speakers; ventilation is planned so equipment does not cook behind closed doors; and the screen height is set from your sofa, not from a generic diagram. Panels or tile then wrap the composition so the wall looks intentional from every angle - including from the kitchen, which is where open-plan homes actually view it from.",
